  "notes": "Boss tutorial. Route: start, door1 (up) into Lair = 1st attack (up sword). Leave via gap at bottom, room3, left door (up), corridor, room4, flip bottom. Back (printed upside down, so after the bottom flip doorDown reads up): end room, doorDown, spin room; spin so doorRight points up (card turned 90 CCW), corridor to west room, flip left; front: east room, door3 (right, now up), room3, re-enter Lair in the 'right' orientation = 2nd sword, boss defeated. No explicit exit; win = defeating the boss. Same layout as the other black-board BOSSRULES translations; door1 at (0.26,0.205), unlike the English green BOSSRULES (0.19,0.25). Unsure: thick double chalk strips (e.g. y 0.26-0.28 under the start box) read as walls, not corridors; the region right of the start box/lair (x>0.94) treated as off-maze.",
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "type": "boss",
      "text": "Defeat the BOSS: enter the Lair in all of the correct orientations in sequence. The swords show the correct orientation and sequence (1: up, 2: right). Leave the Lair by any path and return with the next orientation. If you ever return into the Lair in the incorrect orientation, the BOSS ATTACKS you; if the BOSS has more ATTACKS on you than you have on it, you lose."
    }
  ],
